      "message": "\u003e Patch Set 4:\n\u003e \n\u003e This seems to be reverting an important part of CL:2250092\n\u003e Won\u0027t this cause a regression in the situation when both sides apply Rp?\n\nThis was based on input from Nuvoton with regards to older CrBooks and I added it as a just in case. We are not currently seeing this as being an issue and the current TCPMv2 code performs PS_RDY at the correct time.  So this would be to allow older CrBooks to DUT-DUT connect/charge and the probability is not very high even within that small use case.  I think it is more important to change to allow for TUSB422 to function correctly.\n\nThe most important part of CL:2250092 was the timing of AutoDischargeDisconnect to only be at the times of actual attach.",
